
# CLAUDE.md is TRACKED. It was ignored until 20 August 2026, which meant the
# constraints file that run-all.sh, install.sh, start-session.sh, tmdb.py and
# test_backend.py all cite by number ("constraint 7", "constraint 25") did not
# survive a clone — every one of those comments pointed at a file the deployed
# checkout did not have.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent scratch: `git worktree add` targets land here and are not part of the
# project. Committing one nests a whole second checkout inside this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-user agent settings. `.claude/settings.json` beside it IS tracked — that
# one is the project's shared permission allowlist. This one is personal, and
# was ignored only by a global gitignore until 20 August 2026, which is not
# something a fresh clone on another machine inherits.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-box config. The repo is run in place, so this is how local decisions
# (coordinates, app choices) survive a git pull. server.py prefers it over
# server/config.json when it exists.
server/config.local.json

# The old ee3 catalogue cache and its credentials. Both are gone as of the
# July 2026 remodel — the catalogue is a live Cinemeta call with an in-memory
# TTL, and there is no login anywhere any more. Kept ignored so an old working
# copy that still has these files does not offer them up on the next commit.
server/ee3.env
*.tsv.tmp
cabletv/library.tsv
